WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.010
In ancient China, letters were sent by pigeons and packages by horses.
在中国古代，信件靠鸽子传送，包裹靠马匹运送。

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.820
Common people could hardly afford it.
普通百姓几乎负担不起。

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:13.670
In 1896, China opened its very first post office.
1896年，中国开办了自己的第一家邮局。

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.300
That was the beginning of China’s own postal service.
中国自己的邮政服务由此开始。

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:23.140
With a small stamp on the cover, people in big cities could send letters and packages.
只要在封皮上贴一枚小小的邮票，大城市的人就能寄送信件和包裹了。

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:29.550
Bikes, ships and trains carried them across mountains and rivers in the country, even abroad.
自行车、轮船和火车载着这些信件和包裹，跨越国内的山山水水，甚至运到国外。

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:36.750
After the founding of the People’s Republic of China in 1949, the postal service grew rapidly.
1949年中华人民共和国成立后，邮政服务发展迅速。

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:40.320
Post offices were set up all around the country.
全国各地都设立了邮局。

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.720
Their services stretched to even the quietest, farthest villages.
邮局的服务甚至延伸到了最僻静、最偏远的村庄。

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.650
That made communication much easier for people in every corner of the country.
这让全国各个角落的人们通信方便了许多。

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.950
College students could write to their parents in faraway hometowns.
大学生可以给远在家乡的父母写信了。

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:59.050
Friends and relatives could send packages on festivals to greet each other.
亲朋好友可以在节日里寄送包裹，互致问候。

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:06.760
Since the 1990s, a new branch of postal service, the delivery industry, has also grown rapidly.
自20世纪90年代以来，邮政服务的一个新分支——快递业也迅速发展起来。

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.930
Take the year 2025 for example.
以2025年为例。

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:14.530
Every second, over 6,000 packages were on the move.
每秒钟都有6000多件包裹在运送途中。

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:20.740
Every day, more than 500 million packages were processed and put into trucks.
每天有5亿多件包裹经过处理后装上卡车。

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.210
In the whole year, over 180 billion were sent across the country.
全年寄往全国各地的包裹超过1800亿件。

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:29.840
And the fastest delivery took only several hours!
而且最快的快递只用了几个小时！

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.900
Now, “speed” is no longer the only key word in this industry.
如今，“速度”已不再是这个行业唯一的关键词。

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.710
Many delivery services have started to go green.
许多快递服务已经开始走向绿色环保。

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:43.320
Each year, more than 800 million boxes are reused or recycled.
每年有8亿多个箱子得到重复使用或回收利用。

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:46.840
Besides, smart packing models are widely used.
此外，智能打包模式得到广泛应用。

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:52.970
There’s no doubt that delivery services are smart in our life and friendly to our environment.
毫无疑问，我们生活中的快递服务既智能，又对环境友好。

00:01:53.770 --> 00:02:01.570
From pigeons and horses to delivery trucks, China’s postal history shows how this great old nation has developed and progressed.
从鸽子、马匹到快递卡车，中国邮政的历史展现了这个古老而伟大的国家是怎样发展、进步的。

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:08.230
Looking forward, will China’s postal service fly to the moon and other planets in outer space?
展望未来，中国的邮政服务会飞向月球和外太空的其他星球吗？
